From d7bbf723a6d62c39658211af53e271c9291c736f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:31:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(import): mesh rational B-spline thread strips closed
 and at full fidelity

A thread flank or root exported as one rational strip (degree 1 across,
degree 2 along in 36-degree arcs, ~14 turns) meshed into ~2 M facets with
a 0.5-3 mm hole. Three causes, fixed in the importer's face wrapper:

- step_division: split a parameter direction only where it is curved
  (truck's division split both directions of every failing cell, so a
  strip curved along v got 2^sweeps intervals across u). A division still
  splitting after 64 sweeps (a jump) exhausts the face's evaluation
  budget and is refused by name as before.
- step_stretch: stretch the faster parameter of a B-spline/NURBS face by
  its speed ratio (> 4:1), so truck's Delaunay trimming triangulation
  works in a plane with the face's proportions.
- step_nearest: an answer from truck's parameter search that lies off the
  surface or outside the knot domain is searched again from a sample grid
  with points in every knot span; the nearest answer inside the domain
  wins when it is on the surface or nearer.

10208.STEP: 6.1 M facets / 31-72 s -> 13,662 facets / 1.9 s at 0.005 mm;
32050.STEP: 5.0 M / 62-130 s -> 8,128 / 1.7 s; both close under #1576's
closed-shell check.

Fixes #1602

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
